WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.520
Play!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.570
Oops.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.360
Safe! Safe!

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.020
My error?

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.800
Are you serious?

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.960
Is my fielding percentage gonna go down because he sucks?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.010
I can't do this.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.550
Hey, come over here for a second!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.340
Why did you just shrug?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.550
Again?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.570
You're the one who can't throw well!

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.580
And you're blaming me?

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.690
You...

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.230
What about it?

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.250
Give it a break, Murdoch.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.380
You don't believe in anyone.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.070
So stop getting pissed off about every little thing.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.780
It's not like you have to trust your teammates.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.700
But let me tell you this:

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.050
If you're a professional, complain <i>after</i> you've proven yourself to your teammates!

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.670
Your opponent isn't a teammate, the umpire, or the coaches, old man!

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.670
You son of a...!

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.610
Papa!

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.890
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.890
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:36.190
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:36.190
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:41.570
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:41.570
the only thing I truly have

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:46.860
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:46.860
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.200
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.200
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.460
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.460
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.840
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.840
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:08.930
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:08.930
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:14.480
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:14.480
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.560
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.560
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.860
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.860
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:30.120
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:30.120
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.790
namida kareru made

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.790
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.840
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.840
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.170
namida hareru made

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.170
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.180
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.180
though I may lose my way,

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.020
egakikake no ima

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.020
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.520
kizamu

00:02:55.020 --> 00:03:02.270
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.810
akashi

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:02.270
kono te de

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:08.040
The Responsibility of an Ace

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:08.040
The Responsibility of an Ace

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.720
I want to see you be the best, and smile on the baseball field.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.300
Hey, what's going on?

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.980
Stop what you're doing, Murdoch.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.290
Do you want to be ejected for delay of game?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.990
Goodness.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:40.240
It looks like we'll have to let him cool off in the minors.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:45.220
I placed my hopes in his obstinance as a major leaguer,

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.160
but I was naive.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.410
He forced his own error on someone else.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.370
That's definitely the end for Murdoch.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.070
Now hitting, number 8: Baker!

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.810
Ball.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.250
If you're a professional, complain <i>after</i> you've proven yourself to your teammates!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:23.900
Your opponent isn't a teammate, the umpire, or the coaches, old man!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:25.820
Ball.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:27.950
Ball.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.870
Ball.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.080
Ball four.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.330
That's one out with runners on first and second.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.740
Shigeno's already tired from pitching all out from the start,

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:48.800
and now Murdoch's messed up his rhythm too.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.270
Hey, Sanders, can you catch?

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.680
Oh, sure.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.200
Damn it!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.120
Your pitches have slowed down.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.540
You must be tired from throwing over 100 pitches today.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.510
Want to switch out?

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.510
My pitches have slowed down?

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.550
I'm tired?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.610
Please, you must be kidding.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.260
I clearly don't think that, so a coach shouldn't make me think I am.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.900
No, but...

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:37.070
How many relief pitchers have we burnt out in the past few games?

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:42.250
Hagan and Grissom were both saying their shoulders and elbows are beat.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.400
We can't strain them anymore.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.810
I get six days off and only start from time to time,

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.300
so how could I leave the mound after just six innings?

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.770
Fine.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.970
But if you can't get Howard out, I'm taking you out.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.130
Sure.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.340
Play!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:18.640
When I couldn't pitch because of the yips, I put a lot of burden on the relief pitchers.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.150
The outfielders also helped.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.900
In order to get the team to the top,

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.410
I have to pay my debt to them.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.660
Strike!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.450
Strike!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.310
Strike out!

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.420
Let's go!

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.410
100 mph when he's already pitched six innings.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.010
Unbelievable.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.180
Now hitting, number 15: Patrick!

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:01.980
Ball.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.440
Strike!

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.030
Strike out!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.750
Wow! Goro's amazing!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.420
He's quite the guy.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.100
You saw their pitcher hit me.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.430
You better not forget to get them back.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.640
And don't aim for some soft spot.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.680
Chest or higher.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.810
You can even hit him in the head.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.910
Huh, was I wrong?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.120
I thought he was just a wimp who couldn't even throw a payback pitch.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.040
In any case,

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:08.840
you're not going to make your new teammate feel welcome, right?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.980
Okay, okay.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.260
I get it. Very well.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.070
My fingers were just a little sticky!

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.180
Stop! Both of you!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.510
You better be kidding me!

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:24.600
This is bad.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.540
Then before you try to make someone hit a batter,

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.970
do your own job and stop sucking!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.930
Wh-What did you say?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.450
You bastard...

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.530
Go to hell!

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.380
Murdoch, you're out of here!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:51.870
Damn it!

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:54.050
That kid's unbelievable!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.890
Hey, Murdoch.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.240
Keene twisted his ankle because of you.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.820
He's in the medical room, so don't forget to apologize to him.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.240
Murdoch.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.250
You twisted your ankle from that little fight?

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.200
Man, give me a break!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.470
I didn't do a thing to you.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.750
See ya.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:28.790
Murdoch.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.630
You're probably mad, so maybe this won't get through to you,

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:38.760
but don't criticize Shigeno for not throwing a payback pitch.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.600
What?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:47.080
When he was little, his father died from a pitch to the head.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.290
What about it?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.630
That doesn't have anything to do with me!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.550
No, it doesn't.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:01.560
But I'm saying, it's not cowardice stopping Shigeno from throwing a payback pitch.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.850
Nor is it because he doesn't think you're part of the team.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:10.360
He focuses on winning more than anyone else.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.820
His idea of the best revenge is to strike out the batters.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.220
There's no other payback for him.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:25.520
Ball.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:28.230
Now it's 2-3.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.070
What's his pitch count now?

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.650
The next one will be the 120th pitch.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.380
Damn.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:40.070
I'm getting tired from going all out from the start.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.640
I'm losing control of my pitches.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:47.430
But we can't lose this game, no matter what.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.580
I need to hold out here, or it's pointless.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.080
Pass, Murdoch!

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.000
Out!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.710
Yes!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.380
Papa! Great going!

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:41.880
It's been years since I last saw him play like that.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.430
Good going.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.750
Nice play.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.140
You're so slow to cover the base.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.330
I could've done it faster on my own.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.090
It's the bottom of the eighth with no runs scored,

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.940
and the Panthers have just one out with runners on second and third.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.510
The pitchers must be tired from this action-packed game.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:32.430
Shigeno left the mound after the seventh inning, then Grissom allowed some runners on base.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:37.360
Hagan isn't doing much better, and the count is 0-2 for the fourth batter, Howard.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.060
Geez...

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:44.290
Shigeno held them down for seven innings with his spirit.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:48.280
I can't allow any runs now!

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:53.040
Out!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:54.670
Damn!

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.210
Safe!

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:05.130
They got a run this late in the game.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.840
Damn.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:10.060
Those relief pitchers are too exhausted from the recent games.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.310
Strike out!

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:24.190
The Coyotes won again?

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:29.530
And the Panthers have brought out Del Monte, their closer.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.270
Well, it's hopeless.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.910
We can't win this game.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.070
Now we're seven games behind the lead.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:38.060
It's gonna be impossible to catch up.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:40.420
This season's definitely over for us.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.380
These two are still...

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.590
Hey!

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:47.900
Who just said our season's over?

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:50.010
Oh, I didn't say anything.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:54.180
Damn right you didn't.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:57.320
Considering we're the ones who decide how the season goes,

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.180
people who play here should never give up.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.170
What are you saying?

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.750
You can't do it, Roy.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:13.240
Del Monte has been saving every game this season.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.870
You're gonna need a lot of luck to even get a hit.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.590
Now hitting, number 2: Roy!

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:26.050
Play!

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.660
Damn it...

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.380
We're so pathetic.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:33.470
We've been making the pitchers decide just about every game.

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:36.370
So what if Keene and Greene aren't here?

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.760
If the season ends before they come back,

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.230
then that's just way too lame!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.070
All right! A runner on and no outs!

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.660
He got a hit!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.070
Man, Roy did it.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.830
Now hitting, number 3: Nelson!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.420
Like I'm gonna let Roy hog the spotlight.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.010
Out!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.140
All right!

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:09.090
Nice bunt!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.500
Yeah, we got this!

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.010
Another hit!

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.100
Shigeno's spirit is contagious.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:20.640
The same thing happened on the Bats.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:25.320
His fighting spirit led the team to victory.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:32.320
Now hitting, number 28: Dunstan!

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.070
That sacrifice fly...

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:39.500
We could've gotten him out if I had thrown better.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.120
I'll have to make up for that with this at-bat!

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:49.830
Out!

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.840
Damn it!

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:01.980
Now hitting, number 11: Parker!

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:09.390
Play!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.550
A... walk?

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.480
This is tough.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:20.750
It's the second walk this game.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.170
Papa...

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.160
Ball.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.020
Ball four!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:33.820
Boss.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:34.470
What?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.600
We should switch out Murdoch for a pinch hitter.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.040
I guess we should.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.130
Murdoch hasn't had a single hit in his past four at-bats.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.480
The fans wouldn't like him coming out either.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.100
Umpire—

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.730
Murdoch!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:56.000
Don't let your old teammates make a fool out of you!

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.160
If you're a man, then pay them back!

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:01.600
You're on the Hornets now, Murdoch!

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:02.790
Save your teammates!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:06.290
Take revenge on the Panthers for kicking you out!

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.630
Shigeno's right!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.080
Murdoch, hit one out of the park!

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:16.800
Murdoch!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.900
Give us a run, Murdoch!

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:21.790
Go!

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.640
Show them no mercy!

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:24.600
Hit it like a man!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:32.350
Boss.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.490
I had almost forgotten.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:38.730
I allowed him this game to prove himself.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.910
It wouldn't be fair to switch him out now.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:41.960
Boss!

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.190
Now hitting, number 33:

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:50.230
Mike Murdoch!{lol, full name for him}

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.520
Hello?

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.180
O-Owner?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.020
Play!

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:10.690
You're gonna pay us back?

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.450
Your teammates are dumb.

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:17.120
You're never gonna hit in a situation like this considering your simple-mindedness.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.530
If you could, you wouldn't have been kicked off the team.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.800
Stacy!

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:25.000
I thought I told you to kick that curse out of the game!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.990
What's going on?

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:29.350
Why is he in the batter's box?

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:31.610
Especially at a time like this!

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.690
For the team's victory.

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:34.710
What?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:41.640
The only way we'll win is if every member of the team unleashes all his power.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:46.800
As a coach, I want to believe in Murdoch's power.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.740
Don't give me that nonsense!

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:50.350
Please excuse me. We're in the middle of a game.

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:59.460
Y-You useless idiot!

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.240
Strike!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.920
You're still just a giant who can't hit anything to save the team.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.220
You're too tense, you idiot.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.760
Damn it.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.950
You're so simple-minded.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.220
You're not gonna hit a pitch if you're so tense.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.060
Calm down, Murdoch!

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.520
Look at the ball!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.400
Unbelievable...

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.850
I've been in the majors for years and he's giving me advice?

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:41.600
All the teams I've been on treated me like a monster.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:43.780
Ball.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.340
But... he's different.

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:52.710
He takes everyone seriously in order to win the game.

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:56.130
Strike.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:58.500
Aw, this isn't good.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:19:59.880
He's cornered.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.100
In the past...

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.470
I truly enjoyed baseball.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:14.600
With every swing and every pitch I shared joy and sorrow with my teammates.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.400
That was true happiness.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:18.510
Wait a minute!

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.270
My teammates weren't keeping me out of their loop.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:24.110
I was keeping them out of my bubble.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.400
That's why I've...

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.330
Say goodbye!

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.500
...forgotten my love for baseball!

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.060
It's in!

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:55.350
Murdoch made a comeback with a home run!

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.790
Papa! Papa!

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:59.190
You did it!

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:03.800
H-He really did it!

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:04.710
Yeah.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.630
All right, Murdoch!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:11.680
Murdoch, you showed us.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.000
Nice batting.

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:16.770
Nice job, Murdoch.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.770
You had us worried for a second.

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.000
Nice going.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.090
Not bad.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.360
You're the man.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:24.110
Hogging the spotlight, huh?

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:30.810
This team may not be as bad as I thought.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:37.190
Welcome to the Hornets.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:46.070
All right! Guys, follow Murdoch!

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.090
Strike out!

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:55.210
Game over!

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:11.450
Yes?

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:12.530
Keene?

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:14.220
It's me, Watts.

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:18.230
Did you see today's game results?

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:20.400
Yeah.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:26.240
Now we have enough strength to take the league.

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:31.790
The rest is all about how you'll hold the team together.

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:50.590
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:50.590
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:57.310
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:57.310
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:57.520 --> 00:22:58.980
yume wo

00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:02.150
You were chasing your dream.

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:02.150
oikaketeiru

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:04.940
ground no ue ni

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:08.150
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:08.150
ochiru ase ga

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:12.120
mabushikatta yo

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:12.120
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:19.540
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:19.540
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:26.840
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:26.840
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:31.590
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:34.640
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:34.640
onaji ashi ato

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.220
zutto mae kara

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:42.270
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:38.980
kizukazu ni

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:42.270
suki ni natta

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.560
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:49.400
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:49.400
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:51.990
zutto mae kara

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:57.080
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:53.870
otagai ni

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:57.080
hikareteita

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:59.290
kono kimochi wa

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:06.290
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:06.290
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:14.410
Preview

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:14.410
Preview

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:11.620
Let's win the rest of our games!

00:24:11.620 --> 00:24:13.890
It's almost scary seeing how amazing we're playing.

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:15.240
What?

00:24:15.240 --> 00:24:17.370
We're playing the Salmons next?

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:18.190
All right.

00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:21.560
Then we'll take this momentum and crush my old team!

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:24.060
Next time, on Major: Weak Point.

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:26.470
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

